+# Security False-Positive Analysis — CVE-2026-84446 (libheif, Debian trixie)
+
+**CVE-2026-84446** — *not-affected (false positive)*
+
+| Field | Value |
+|-------|-------|
+| CVE | CVE-2026-84446 |
+| Package | `libheif` |
+| Distribution | Debian 13 (trixie) |
+| Shipped version | `1.19.8` (`1.19.8-1+deb13u1`) |
+| Verdict | **not-affected** — vulnerable code not present |
+| Reason class | Feature introduced in the next minor release (1.20.0), after the shipped version |
+| Upstream advisory | https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/security/advisories/GHSA-xw34-mjcp-jqh8 |
+| Upstream fix | https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/commit/3a7a69ae325f652e48c026b8241ab25bedf44d9b |
+
+---
+
+## 1. Summary
+
+CVE-2026-84446 (GHSA-xw34-mjcp-jqh8) reports sequence timing-table DoS and
+unbounded memory in libheif's HEIF image-sequence / track subsystem. A crafted
+sequence with an edit-list repeat plus movie-header duration can amplify a
+single physical sample into an astronomical logical output count; per-track
+tables bypass memory limits; and `Box_stts::get_sample_duration()` is O(entries)
+per sample.
+
+Debian trixie ships **libheif 1.19.8**. The vulnerable code lives in
+`libheif/sequences/` (`track.cc`, `seq_boxes.cc`, `chunk.cc`) and
+`libheif/api/libheif/heif_sequences.cc`. That entire image-sequence / track
+subsystem was introduced in **libheif 1.20.0**, the release after the one
+trixie shipped.
+
+The advisory range `<= 1.23.1` is **numerically true but misleading** for
+1.19.8: `1.19.8 < 1.23.1`, yet none of the affected symbols exist. A crafted
+"HEIF sequence file" cannot reach the vulnerable logic — relevant boxes are
+unknown and skipped by size.
+
+**Conclusion: CVE-2026-84446 is a false positive for trixie and should be marked
+`not-affected`.**
+
+---
+
+## 2. Why quilt cannot apply the upstream patch
+
+The upstream fix (`3a7a69ae`) patches paths that do not exist in 1.19.8:
+
+- `libheif/api/libheif/heif_sequences.cc`
+- `libheif/sequences/chunk.cc` / `chunk.h`
+- `libheif/sequences/seq_boxes.cc` / `seq_boxes.h`
+- `libheif/sequences/track.cc` / `track.h`
+- `tests/sequence_timing_overflow.cc`
+
+`quilt fold` therefore reports `can't find file to patch` for every hunk.
+That failure is expected: there is nothing to backport.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Source verification
+
+```text
+$ ls libheif/sequences   # against v1.19.8 tag
+ls: cannot access 'libheif/sequences': No such file or directory
+
+$ git grep -nE "init_sample_timing_table|Box_stts|heif_sequences" v1.19.8 -- '*.cc' '*.h'
+(no matches)
+
+$ git ls-tree -r --name-only v1.19.8 | grep -iE 'sequence|track\.cc|seq_boxes'
+(no sequence/track/seq_boxes source files in v1.19.8)
+
+# first appearance
+$ git grep -nE "init_sample_timing_table" v1.20.0 -- '*.cc' '*.h'
+v1.20.0:libheif/sequences/track.cc:...
+```
+
+---
+
+## 4. Recommended triage entry
+
+```
+[trixie] - libheif <not-affected> (Image-sequence timing table /
+init_sample_timing_table / Box_stts — introduced in 1.20.0; trixie ships
+1.19.8 which predates the feature)
+```
+
+---
+
